# Claude Code Rules for Enamorado Platform

## File and Directory Inclusion Syntax

Use the `@` syntax to include files and directories in your Gemini prompts:

### File Inclusion
- `@file_name.ext` - Include a specific file
- `@path/to/file.ext` - Include a file with full path
- Multiple files: `@file1.js @file2.ts @file3.css`

### Directory Inclusion
- `@directory_name/` - Include all files in a directory
- `@path/to/directory/` - Include directory with full path
- Recursive: `@directory_name/**` - Include all files recursively

### Pattern Matching
- `@*.js` - Include all JavaScript files in current directory
- `@**/*.tsx` - Include all TypeScript React files recursively
- `@src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` - Include all TypeScript files in src directory

### Examples
```
"Review @src/components/Navigation.tsx and @src/App.tsx"
"Analyze all components: @src/components/"
"Check types: @shared/schema.ts @server/types.ts"
"Fix all pages: @src/pages/**/*.tsx"
```

## Project Structure

### Core Directories
- `client/src/` - React frontend
  - `components/` - Reusable UI components
  - `pages/` - Route pages
  - `hooks/` - Custom React hooks
  - `lib/` - Utility functions
- `server/` - Express backend
  - `routes.ts` - API endpoints (5300+ lines)
  - `index.ts` - Server entry point
  - `storage.ts` - Database operations
- `shared/` - Shared types and schemas
  - `schema.ts` - Database schema (30+ tables)

### Important Files
- `.env` - Environment variables (DO NOT COMMIT)
- `vite.config.ts` - Vite build configuration
- `package.json` - Dependencies
- `PLATFORM_STATUS.md` - Current platform status

## Development Guidelines

### Database Schema
- Radio tables: standard naming (shows, episodes, guides, etc.)
- Magazine/Editorial tables: `editorial_` prefix (editorial_submissions, editorial_content, editorial_issues)
- Unified contributor system shared across both

### API Routes
- Radio: `/api/shows`, `/api/episodes`, `/api/guides`
- Editorial: `/api/submissions`, `/api/content`, `/api/issues`
- Admin: `/api/admin/*` (requires authentication)

### Component Conventions
- Use TypeScript for all new components
- Follow existing shadcn/ui patterns
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling

### Submission System
Unified submission flow supporting:
- DJ mixes (audio files via AzuraCast SFTP)
- Playlists (Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube)
- Artwork (images, photography)
- Writing (essays, poems, PDFs)
- Links/Videos (web content)
- Album suggestions (community voting)

## External Integrations

### AzuraCast (Radio Streaming)
- Base URL: http://24.199.109.18
- Station: enamorado_radio
- SFTP uploads for DJ mixes

### APIs Connected
- Spotify (metadata enrichment)
- Last.fm (scrobbling, recommendations)
- Iframely (rich embeds for 1900+ platforms)
- Google Sheets (resident applications)
- Replit Object Storage (file uploads)

## Common Tasks

### Starting Development
```bash
npm run dev  # Starts on port 8080
```

### Database Operations
```bash
npm run db:push  # Push schema changes
npm run db:studio  # Open Drizzle Studio
```

### Type Checking
```bash
npm run check  # TypeScript type check
```

### Building
```bash
npm run build  # Production build
npm start  # Run production server
```

## Troubleshooting

### Port Conflicts
- Port 5000: macOS Control Center (AirPlay)
- Port 3000: Website inspector tools
- Default: Port 8080

### Missing Dependencies
If build fails with missing imports:
1. Check if component exists in `client/src/components/`
2. Create missing component with proper TypeScript types
3. Ensure imports match actual file structure

### Database Conflicts
- Always use `editorial_` prefix for new magazine tables
- Check PLATFORM_STATUS.md for current schema
- Review DATABASE_SCHEMA_ANALYSIS.md before migrations
